# a call with a list lays the list out on the stack, and throws in front of the callee where the list finds no room. A callee that is handed the list itself as its rest parameter, or nothing of it, would take any list
# so the direct call stands behind a test of the length, and a list that is longer than a call can write out goes by the call as written, out of the way
# function count(...all) { return all.length }  function nothing() { return 0 }
# function returned(list) { return count(...list) }
# Both ways leave by a tail call
# RUN: walk f3 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK: [[list]]: Array {{*}} = NewArray
# CHECK: [[length]]: {{*}} = GetArrayLength [[list]]
# CHECK: [[short]]: boolean {{*}} = LessEq
# CHECK: Branch [[short]] -> taken [[direct]](), notTaken [[written]]()
# CHECK: [[direct]]():
# CHECK: [[entered]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# CHECK: ReturnCall [[entered]]
# CHECK: [[written]]() frequency=Rare:
# CHECK-NEXT: [[called]]: {{*}} = CallList {{*}}, -, [[list]] calleeName="count"
# CHECK-NEXT: ReturnCall [[called]]
# function added(list) { return count(...list) + 1 }
# The two ways meet behind the call
# RUN(ADDED): walk f4 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# ADDED-LABEL: code f4:Body
# ADDED: [[short]]: boolean {{*}} = LessEq
# ADDED: Branch [[short]] -> taken [[direct]](), notTaken [[written]]()
# ADDED: [[direct]]():
# ADDED: [[entered]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# ADDED: Jump -> next [[behind]]([[entered]])
# ADDED: [[written]]() frequency=Rare:
# ADDED-NEXT: [[called]]: {{*}} = CallList
# ADDED-NEXT: Jump -> next [[behind]]([[called]])
# ADDED: [[behind]]([[result]]:
# ADDED: = Add [[result]],
# function ignored(list) { return nothing(...list) }
# RUN(IGNORED): walk f5 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# IGNORED-LABEL: code f5:Body
# IGNORED: = GetArrayLength
# IGNORED: = CallDirect function=f2
# IGNORED: = CallList
# function listed(a, b) { return count(...[a, b]) }
# The control: the text says how long the list is, so nothing is asked
# RUN(LISTED): walk f6 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# LISTED-LABEL: code f6:Body
# LISTED-NOT: GetArrayLength
# LISTED-NOT: CallList
# LISTED: [[entered]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# LISTED: ReturnCall [[entered]]
# with every mechanism on the lengths are compared as integers. The callee returns a raw number and the caller, which anybody may call, a boxed one: the direct call comes back and boxes, the rare way is a jump
# RUN(ALL): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# ALL-LABEL: code f3:Body
# ALL: = LessEq {{*}}form=Integers
# ALL: [[entered]]: {{*}} @Double = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# ALL-NEXT: [[boxed]]: {{*}} @JSValue = Box [[entered]]
# ALL-NEXT: Return [[boxed]]
# ALL: [[called]]: {{*}} @JSValue = CallList
# ALL-NEXT: ReturnCall [[called]]
# with direct calls withheld there is the call as written and no test
# RUN(CLOSED): walk f3 mechanisms=none
# CLOSED-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CLOSED-NOT: GetArrayLength
# CLOSED: [[called]]: {{*}} = CallList
# CLOSED-NEXT: ReturnCall [[called]]

variable g0 name="count" module=m0 declared={type=f1 flags=[IsFromCompiler]} initialization=Function function=f1 flags=[IsImmutable]
variable g1 name="nothing" module=m0 declared={type=f2 flags=[IsFromCompiler]} initialization=Function function=f2 flags=[IsImmutable]
module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
